From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshijiang <ssj1595329871@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] configs: lckfb-tspi-rk3566: enable HAOS required options

The upstream lckfb-tspi-rk3566_defconfig is a plain board config. The
Home Assistant OS boot script (uboot-boot.ush) additionally needs:

  - CONFIG_CMD_PART   : "part start"/"part number" to locate the
                         hassos-boot/hassos-kernel0/hassos-kernel1
                         partitions by GPT partition number.
  - CONFIG_CMD_FAT    : "fatload" to read haos-config.txt, cmdline.txt and
                         the device tree from the vfat boot partition.
  - CONFIG_CMD_FILEENV: "fileenv" to source cmdline.txt into ${cmdline}.

CONFIG_PARTITIONS itself is pulled in by CONFIG_EFI_PARTITION, which the
shared HAOS bootloader fragment (buildroot-external/bootloader/uboot.config)
already enables.

Also enable HS200 for the eMMC. On RK356x boards, DDR52 mode is known to
produce corrupt eMMC writes; only HS200 works reliably. This mirrors the
upstream Home Assistant Green board patch "green: Do not use eMMC DDR52
mode, enable HS200".

Signed-off-by: sunshijiang <ssj1595329871@gmail.com>
---
 configs/lckfb-tspi-rk3566_defconfig | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/configs/lckfb-tspi-rk3566_defconfig b/configs/lckfb-tspi-rk3566_defconfig
index b5479fd..42d7ee7 100644
--- a/configs/lckfb-tspi-rk3566_defconfig
+++ b/configs/lckfb-tspi-rk3566_defconfig
@@ -58,6 +58,8 @@ CONFIG_DM_PMIC=y
 CONFIG_DM_PMIC_FAN53555=y
 CONFIG_PMIC_RK8XX=y
 CONFIG_REGULATOR_RK8XX=y
+CONFIG_MMC_HS200_SUPPORT=y
+CONFIG_SPL_MMC_HS200_SUPPORT=y
 CONFIG_SPL_RAM=y
 CONFIG_BAUDRATE=1500000
 CONFIG_DEBUG_UART_SHIFT=2
@@ -69,6 +71,9 @@ CONFIG_USB_XHCI_HCD=y
 CONFIG_USB_XHCI_GENERIC=y
 CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD=y
 CONFIG_USB_EHCI_GENERIC=y
+CONFIG_CMD_PART=y
+CONFIG_CMD_FAT=y
+CONFIG_CMD_FILEENV=y
 CONFIG_USB_DWC3=y
 CONFIG_USB_DWC3_GENERIC=y
 CONFIG_USB_GADGET=y
